RESULT {"run": "smoke-fu-e88f0806-r1", "case": "gobwas-ws-a567dfd6", "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "outcome": "finished", "model_calls": 12, "tool_calls": 12, "in_tok": 26, "cache_write": 21716, "cache_read": 68189, "out_tok": 6286, "model_s": 53.63, "tool_s": 615.5, "commands": [{"cmd": "cd wsflate && grep -rn \"stream tail\" . | head; git log --oneline | head -3; git status --short", "rc": 0, "s": 0.21}, {"cmd": "cd wsflate && sed -n 1,160p writer.go; grep -n \"tail\\|Tail\" *.go | grep -v _test", "rc": 0, "s": 0.08}, {"cmd": "cd wsflate && cat cbuf.go", "rc": 0, "s": 0.08}, {"cmd": "cd wsflate && sed -n 1,80p ../tests/deflate_test.go | head -5; grep -n \"Close\\|Flush\" ../tests/deflate_test.go helper.go | head -20", "rc": 0, "s": 0.1}, {"cmd": "cd wsflate && sed -n 150,200p helper.go; grep -n \"func.*Compressor\\|flate\\.\" *.go | grep -v _test", "rc": 0, "s": 0.08}, {"cmd": "cd wsflate && python3 - <<'E'\ns=open('writer.go').read()\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"\t\tw.err = c.Close()\n\t}\n\tw.checkTail()\n\"\"\",\"\"\"\t\tw.err = c.Close()\n\t}\n\"\"\")\nopen('writer.go','w').write(s)\nE\ncd .. && go test -count=1 github.com/gobwas/ws/tests github.com/gobwas/ws/wsflate 2>&1 | tail -15", "rc": 127, "s": 0.11}, {"cmd": "export PATH=$PATH:/usr/local/go/bin:~/go/bin; go test -count=1 github.com/gobwas/ws/tests github.com/gobwas/ws/wsflate 2>&1 | tail -15", "rc": 124, "s": 600.11}, {"cmd": "export PATH=$PATH:/usr/local/go/bin; cd /srv/ci/cases/gobwas-ws-a567dfd6/repo; git diff --stat; timeout 120 go test -count=1 -timeout 30s github.com/gobwas/ws/wsflate 2>&1 | head -40", "rc": 1, "s": 6.26}, {"cmd": "cd /srv/ci/cases/gobwas-ws-a567dfd6/repo; git checkout wsflate/writer.go; cat wsflate/writer_test.go | head -60; sed -n 1,40p wsflate/helper.go", "rc": 0, "s": 0.26}, {"cmd": "cd /srv/ci/cases/gobwas-ws-a567dfd6/repo; export PATH=$PATH:/usr/local/go/bin; go version; cat go.mod; ls; ls wsflate; git status --short; grep -n \"Close\" -B3 -A15 wsflate/reader.go | head -60", "rc": 0, "s": 0.36}, {"cmd": "cd /srv/ci/cases/gobwas-ws-a567dfd6/repo; export PATH=$PATH:/usr/local/go/bin; mkdir /tmp/x && cat > /tmp/x/main_test.go <<'E'\npackage x\nimport (\"testing\";\"bytes\";\"compress/flate\";\"fmt\")\nfunc TestX(t *testing.T){\n var b bytes.Buffer\n w,_:=flate.NewWriter(&b,9)\n w.Write([]byte(\"hello\"))\n w.Flush(); fmt.Printf(\"% x\\n\",b.Bytes())\n w.Close(); fmt.Printf(\"% x\\n\",b.Bytes())\n}\nE\ncd /tmp/x && cat > go.mod", "rc": 0, "s": 3.11}, {"cmd": "cd /srv/ci/cases/gobwas-ws-a567dfd6/repo; export PATH=$PATH:/usr/local/go/bin; python3 - <<'E'\ns=open('wsflate/writer.go').read()\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"\tif c, ok := w.c.(io.Closer); ok {\n\t\tw.err = c.Close()\n\t}\n\tw.checkTail()\n\treturn w.err\"\"\",\"\"\"\t// The stream must already be terminated by the sync flush tail. Whatever\n\t// the compressor emits on Close() (such as final empty block) is not part\n\t// of the ", "rc": 0, "s": 4.72}], "final_text": "The test command now passes for both `tests` and `wsflate`.\n\n**Cause:** `wsflate.Writer` strips the last 4 bytes of the compressed stream (the `00 00 ff ff` sync-flush tail) with `cbuf`. `Close()` then ran `checkTail()` after calling the compressor's `Close()`. Current `compress/flate` writes a final empty block (`03 00`) when closed. That pushed `ff ff 03 00` into the tail buffer. As a result, `checkTail()` failed with \"unexpected stream tail\". The helper's `Flush()` followed by `Close()` therefore failed in `TestWriter`, `TestHelperWriteAndRead` and `TestFlateClientServer`.\n\n**Fix (`wsflate/writer.go`):** `Close()` now checks the tail first, while it is still the flush tail. It then redirects `cbuf` output to `ioutil.Discard` before closing the compressor. The extra final-block bytes are not part of the permessage-deflate payload, so they are dropped. Closing without a prior `Flush()` still returns an error.\n\nMy first attempt was to remove `checkTail()` from `Close()`. That produced corrupt output, so I reverted it. I wasn't able to confirm what the upstream project does here, so this fix is my own design rather than a copy of upstream.\n\nMy first run of the test command under a plain `go test` timed out after 600 s, so I didn't get its output. I reran with `-timeout 60s` and it finished in under a second. I didn't find out why the first run hung. It may have been related to my first attempted change.", "patch": "diff --git a/wsflate/writer.go b/wsflate/writer.go\nindex 0342ccb..d6e937f 100644\n--- a/wsflate/writer.go\n+++ b/wsflate/writer.go\n@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@ package wsflate\n import (\n \t\"fmt\"\n \t\"io\"\n+\t\"io/ioutil\"\n )\n \n var (\n@@ -104,13 +105,20 @@ func (w *Writer) Flush() error {\n // Close closes Writer and a Compressor instance used under the hood (if it\n // implements io.Closer interface).\n func (w *Writer) Close() error {\n+\tif w.err != nil {\n+\t\treturn w.err\n+\t}\n+\t// The stream must already be terminated by the sync flush tail. Whatever\n+\t// the compressor emits on Close() (such as final empty block) is not part\n+\t// of the permessage-deflate payload, so it is discarded.\n+\tw.checkTail()\n \tif w.err != nil {\n \t\treturn w.err\n \t}\n \tif c, ok := w.c.(io.Closer); ok {\n+\t\tw.cbuf.dst = ioutil.Discard\n \t\tw.err = c.Close()\n \t}\n-\tw.checkTail()\n \treturn w.err\n }\n \n", "total_s": 669.97}
